  "notes": "Provenance and licensing. (1) Icons: the bulk are the \"win98icons\" catalogue by Alex Meub (win98icons.alexmeub.com) -- PNG renders of the icon resources shipped inside Windows 98 (shell32.dll, pifmgr.dll, main.cpl and friends), which is why they are authentic 16-colour 32x32/16x16 art. A few (run, logoff, pinball) come from the github.com/1j01/98 icon folder, which carries the same catalogue plus community additions. The catalogue is distributed freely by its author and the repo is a shared-source project; the underlying artwork is Microsoft copyright and is used here for a non-commercial period reproduction. (2) @react95/icons (MIT, npm @react95/icons 2.5.3) was evaluated as a secondary source but not needed -- the authentic catalogue covered more keys. (3) Cursors: the arrow, crosshair, move and the four resize cursors are the real Microsoft system cursor bitmaps as carried by jspaint (github.com/1j01/98, programs/jspaint/images/cursors). The remaining cursors are reconstructed here as 32x32 black-with-white-outline pixel art. (4) Sounds: eleven files are the unmodified Windows 98 \\MEDIA WAV files (The Microsoft Sound, CHIMES, CHORD, DING, TADA, LOGOFF, NOTIFY, RECYCLE) recovered via github.com/MCPlayer2015/all-windows-sounds, a repository of Microsoft audio that states Microsoft copyright. Windows 98 mapped Asterisk/Question to CHIMES.WAV and Critical Stop/Exclamation to CHORD.WAV, so error/exclamation/question are byte-identical copies of chord/chime -- that is the real Windows 98 behaviour, not a stub. The nine sounds marked \"synthesised\": true are 22.05 kHz 16-bit mono PCM written by this build because Windows 98 shipped no sound for window minimise/maximise/close/restore, menu, click, logon, shutdown or balloon events. (5) Wallpapers: clouds, setup and every tiled pattern are the genuine Windows 98 BMP files recovered via github.com/Kippykip/W9X-Wallpapers (Microsoft copyright). windows98.png is the authentic Clouds.bmp with the Windows 98 branding lockup drawn on top. slate, honeycomb, marbled and lattice are synthesised 2-colour tiled patterns because no BMP was recoverable. (6) logo and boot are drawn here (PIL pixel/polygon art, no anti-aliasing) as faithful reconstructions. All artwork is hard-edged 1998-style: 16-colour icons, 1-bit cursors, no gradients, no anti-aliasing, no modern or emoji imagery. Every file is local; nothing is fetched at runtime."
}